{"text":"kuruntokai","n":315,"lines":["எழுதரு மதியங் கடற்கண் டாஅங்","கொழுகுவெள் ளருவி யோங்குமலை நாடன்","ஞாயி றனையன் தோழி","நெருஞ்சி யனையவென் பெரும்பணைத் தோளே"],"tr":["eḻutaru matiyaṅ kaṭaṟkaṇ ṭāaṅ","koḻukuveḷ ḷaruvi yōṅkumalai nāṭaṉ","ñāyi ṟaṉaiyaṉ tōḻi","neruñci yaṉaiyaveṉ perumpaṇait tōḷē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"kuṟiñci","tinai_ta":"குறிஞ்சி","speaker_ta":"தலைவி கூற்று","poet_ta":"மதுரை வேள்ஆதத்தனார்","speaker_en":"the heroine (talaivi)","poet_tr":"Maturai Vēḷātattaṉār"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 14, veṇcīr 1"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 7, veṇṭaḷai 7"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"எழுதரு","tr":"eḻutaru","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"எழு","tr":"eḻu"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"தரு","tr":"taru"}]},{"text":"மதியங்","tr":"matiyaṅ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"மதி","tr":"mati"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யங்","tr":"yaṅ"}]},{"text":"கடற்கண்","tr":"kaṭaṟkaṇ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"கடற்","tr":"kaṭaṟ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கண்","tr":"kaṇ"}]},{"text":"டாஅங்","tr":"ṭāaṅ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"டா","tr":"ṭā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"அங்","tr":"aṅ"}]}],[{"text":"கொழுகுவெள்","tr":"koḻukuveḷ","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"கொழு","tr":"koḻu"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"குவெள்","tr":"kuveḷ"}]},{"text":"ளருவி","tr":"ḷaruvi","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"ளரு","tr":"ḷaru"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வி","tr":"vi"}]},{"text":"யோங்குமலை","tr":"yōṅkumalai","foot":"kūviḷaṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யோங்","tr":"yōṅ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"கும","tr":"kuma"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"லை","tr":"lai"}]},{"text":"நாடன்","tr":"nāṭaṉ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நா","tr":"nā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"டன்","tr":"ṭaṉ"}]}],[{"text":"ஞாயி","tr":"ñāyi","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"ஞா","tr":"ñā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யி","tr":"yi"}]},{"text":"றனையன்","tr":"ṟaṉaiyaṉ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"றனை","tr":"ṟaṉai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யன்","tr":"yaṉ"}]},{"text":"தோழி","tr":"tōḻi","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தோ","tr":"tō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ழி","tr":"ḻi"}]}],[{"text":"நெருஞ்சி","tr":"neruñci","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"நெருஞ்","tr":"neruñ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"சி","tr":"ci"}]},{"text":"யனையவென்","tr":"yaṉaiyaveṉ","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"யனை","tr":"yaṉai"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"யவென்","tr":"yaveṉ"}]},{"text":"பெரும்பணைத்","tr":"perumpaṇait","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பெரும்","tr":"perum"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"பணைத்","tr":"paṇait"}]},{"text":"தோளே","tr":"tōḷē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தோ","tr":"tō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளே","tr":"ḷē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"எழுதரு","parts":[{"text":"எழுதரு","lemma":"எழுதரு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மதியங்","parts":[{"text":"மதியங்","lemma":"மதியங்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கடற்கண்","parts":[{"text":"கடற்கண்","lemma":"கடற்கண்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"டாஅங்","parts":[{"text":"டாஅங்","lemma":"டாஅங்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"கொழுகு","parts":[{"text":"கொழுகு","lemma":"கொழுகு","gloss":"gushing"}],"gloss":"gushing"},{"surface":"வெள்","parts":[{"text":"வெள்","lemma":"வெள்","gloss":"white"}],"gloss":"white"},{"surface":"அருவி","parts":[{"text":"அருவி","lemma":"அருவி","gloss":"waterfall"}],"gloss":"waterfall"},{"surface":"ஓங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஓங்கு","lemma":"ஓங்கு","gloss":"lofty"}],"gloss":"lofty"},{"surface":"மலை","parts":[{"text":"மலை","lemma":"மலை","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"mountain"},{"surface":"நாடன்","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"land"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"lord of the land"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஞாயிறு","parts":[{"text":"ஞாயிறு","lemma":"ஞாயிறு","gloss":"sun"}],"gloss":"sun"},{"surface":"அனையன்","parts":[{"text":"அனையன்","lemma":"அனையன்","gloss":"he is like"}],"gloss":"he is like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"தோழி","gloss":"friend"}],"gloss":"O friend"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெருஞ்சி","parts":[{"text":"நெருஞ்சி","lemma":"நெருஞ்சி","gloss":"puncture-vine"}],"gloss":"puncture-vine flower"},{"surface":"அனைய","parts":[{"text":"அனைய","lemma":"அனைய","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"பெரும்பணை","parts":[{"text":"பெரும்பணை","lemma":"பெரும்பணை","gloss":"large bamboo-like"}],"gloss":"large bamboo-like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தோளே","parts":[{"text":"தோள்","lemma":"தோள்","gloss":"shoulder"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"shoulders indeed"}]}],"literal":"Like seeing the rising moon in the sea, / the lord of the land of lofty mountains with gushing white waterfalls, / is like the sun, O friend! / My large, bamboo-like shoulders are like the puncture-vine flower.","translation":"Like seeing the rising moon over the ocean is the lord of the lofty mountains where white waterfalls gush. He is like the sun, my friend, and my large, bamboo-like shoulders are like the puncture-vine flower.","modern":"அலைகள் வீசும் கடலில் உதிக்கின்ற முழு நிலவைக் காண்பது போல, வெள்ளிய அருவிகள் கொட்டுகின்ற உயர்ந்த மலைநாட்டை உடைய தலைவன் விளங்குகிறான். தோழியே! அவன் சூரியனைப் போன்றவன்; என்னுடைய பெரிய மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களோ சூரியனை நோக்கித் திரியும் நெருஞ்சிப் பூவைப் போன்றன.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her deep devotion to the hero. She compares the hero, who rules over the lofty mountains with gushing white waterfalls, to the sun. She compares her own beautiful, bamboo-like shoulders to the puncture-vine (neruñci) flower, which always turns its face to follow the sun. Just as the flower cannot exist without looking at the sun, her beauty and life depend entirely on him. The comparison of the hero to the rising moon over the sea highlights his cool, pleasing nature, while his role as the sun highlights her constant devotion.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}